Description: Rust MCP server for Linux desktop control
 computer-use-linux provides an MCP server that gives AI agents full
 control over a Linux desktop environment via AT-SPI2, Wayland portals,
 and compositor D-Bus APIs.
 .
 Capabilities:
 - Accessibility tree inspection (AT-SPI2)
 - Mouse/keyboard input injection
 - Window management (list, focus, move, resize)
 - Screenshot capture
 - Clipboard access
 - App launching via D-Bus
 - System tray integration
 .
 This is the shared desktop control backend used by both Hermes and
 OpenClaw when running in DuckBotOS. The agent connects as an MCP
 client to this service.
Homepage: https://github.com/agent-sh/computer-use-linux